<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Li Hualong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1554">1554</a>–<a href="/years/1611">1611</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Li Hualong was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming dynasty</a> official who served as supreme commander in the south-west during the reign of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wanli-emperor">Wanli Emperor</a>. In 1600 he led a large army against the rebellious chieftain <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yang-yinglong">Yang Yinglong</a> of Bozhou, storming his fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hailongtun">Hailongtun</a>, in one of the 'three great campaigns' of Wanli's reign. Bozhou was then brought under direct imperial rule.</p></div>
